## Parsing (WebAssembly)

Outline, completion, and Tier B formatting use bundled [web-tree-sitter](https://github.com/tree-sitter/tree-sitter/tree/master/lib/binding_web) (npm `web-tree-sitter@0.24.7`, MIT License) with:

- `src/assets/tree-sitter.wasm` — [tree-sitter/tree-sitter](https://github.com/tree-sitter/tree-sitter) release **v0.24.7** (MIT License).
- `src/assets/tree-sitter-abl.wasm` — [eglekaz/tree-sitter-abl](https://github.com/eglekaz/tree-sitter-abl) via npm `tree-sitter-abl@0.1.2` (MIT License).

Run `npm run fetch:parser-wasm` to re-download these files if needed. The extension does not ship native `tree-sitter` Node bindings.

## Grammar tests (dev only)

Unit tests load TextMate grammars with [vscode-textmate](https://github.com/microsoft/vscode-textmate) and [vscode-oniguruma](https://github.com/microsoft/vscode-oniguruma) (MIT License). These packages are devDependencies and are **not** shipped in the VSIX.

## ADE corpus (tests only)

Regression tests optionally use [progress/ADE](https://github.com/progress/ADE) at branch `release-12.8.x` (Apache License 2.0). The corpus is **not** shipped in the VSIX; it is checked out under `corpus/ade` locally or in CI.
